previousNode.getProperties().put(MOUSE_TRANSPARENT, previousNode.isMouseTransparent());
previousNode.setMouseTransparent(true);
```
Reason:
The handling of the `mouseTransparent` property for `previousNode` was inconsistent. The code attempted to manage the transparency state of `previousNode` individually, which could allow mouse events to be processed by it even when it should not, leading to unexpected interactions in the user interface.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```java
view.setMouseTransparent(false);
view.setMouseTransparent(true);
```
Reason:
The fix involves setting the `mouseTransparent` property for the entire `view` instead of individual nodes. By ensuring that the whole view is set to be mouse transparent during transitions, it prevents any mouse events from being processed by `previousNode`, thus eliminating the unintended interactions.

